+# codEx patch-module manifest.
+#
+# The fork's delta to upstream is organized as exactly one patch per module,
+# applied in the order below. Each section names the module, the exact
+# commit/patch subject, and the files the module owns (paths relative to the
+# tree root, one bash case-pattern per line; `*` matches any characters,
+# including `/`). Every file changed by the fork must match exactly one
+# module - the ownership partition is machine-checked.
+#
+# Workflow rules:
+#   - New feature: append a section here and create the matching commit in
+#     the bootstrapped tree, then run scripts/gen-patches.sh.
+#   - Change to an existing feature: rebase/--fixup the change into that
+#     module's commit, then regenerate. Move a file between sections only
+#     when its ownership actually changes.
+#   - Never hand-edit patches/; scripts/check-patch-modules.sh rejects any
+#     tree or export that violates this manifest.
+
